; Credential_observation — decodes a repo-hosting CLI's own structured status
; output and reports what that credential surface resolves to (RFC-0369).
;
; Decoding goes through Yojson and masc_core's Json_util/Safe_ops accessors.
; An earlier revision hand-parsed gh's human text instead; that text cannot
; carry the failure cause at all (a DNS failure reads as "the token is
; invalid"), and the hand-rolled reader duplicated accessors the repo already
; had in 600 other modules.
;
; Deliberately outside exec, Gate, and policy: those layers must not know a
; particular CLI or credential scheme (INV-KEEPER-008, the reason RFC-0309 was
; withdrawn). This library observes and never acts, so it depends on nothing
; but string utilities.
;
; (include_subdirs no) opts out of the parent's (include_subdirs unqualified).

(include_subdirs no)

(library
 (name masc_credential_observation)
 (public_name masc.credential_observation)
 (wrapped false)
 (modules gh_auth_status)
 (flags
  (:standard -w +4 -w +33))
 (libraries masc_core yojson))
